From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.globalization: the Language statics (1529)

Windows.Globalization.Language answers ILanguageStatics (IsWellFormed,
CurrentInputMethodLanguageTag) and ILanguageStatics2
(TrySetInputMethodLanguageTag) from its activation factory. Wine answered
E_NOINTERFACE. Microsoft Publisher asks for them each time a text box takes
the caret. The input method's language is the thread's keyboard layout;
IsWellFormed checks BCP-47 subtag syntax; TrySet switches to an installed
layout of that language and says FALSE when there is none.

Gate: test/langstatics-gate.sh.
Mutant: SG_MUTANT_LANGUAGE_STATICS_MISSING (gate fails: statics=80004002).
windows.globalization conformance unchanged (77 tests, 0 failures).

